    "dateline": "Sunday, October 19.",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "lead": "A ",
        "bird": "Steller's Jay",
        "plate": 1,
        "rest": " came five mornings out of seven, always before eleven. It takes seed by the beakful to hide, carrying several at once in its throat."
      },
      {
        "lead": "The ",
        "bird": "Black-capped Chickadees",
        "plate": 2,
        "rest": " have come six mornings in a row, usually in pairs. Each one takes a single seed, flies to a branch, and hammers it open, or tucks it into bark to find later."
      },
      {
        "lead": "The ",
        "bird": "House Finches",
        "rest": " still run the place, with more than half of all visits. The juncos came back on Thursday for the first time in months."
      }
    ]
